'' ===========================================================================
''
''   File.......  test-contract-gaps-p1-instruction-flow.spin2
''   Purpose....  Eight instruction-flow questions, arms A to H, each with
''                controls that must come out both ways.  No pins are used.
''   Manual.....  P2 Knowledge Base
''   Authors....  Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''   E-mail.....  stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started....  Nov 2026
''   Updated....  Nov 2026
''
'' ===========================================================================

{ RIG
  Bare P2 board, 200 MHz, NOTHING attached.  No pins are touched.
  Build pnut-ts -d.  Cog 0 supervises and prints; no other cog has the
  debugger.  Every step runs in a fresh worker cog that writes its record to
  hub and DONE last; the supervisor stops a worker that has not finished in
  STEP_MS and reports that step as hung.  Results print before verdicts, and
  every reading not named below is printed raw as OTHER or NO READING.

ARM A  Does a far CALLD PA,#label in hub land on its label?
  The compiler encodes this word with the distance in instructions (-1006).
  A byte reading of that field lands 1006 bytes back, inside a sled whose
  every long, and every 2-byte offset of it, is CALL #\HANDLER; the handler
  reports the address it was called from.
    Control      a far CALL to a label 1005 instructions back lands on it.
    Word 1       the compiler's CALLD.  LABEL, or the sled at the byte reading.
    Word 2       a hand-encoded CALLD whose field is the byte distance (-64).
                 LABEL under a byte reading; under an instruction reading it
                 lands 256 bytes back, in a second sled.
    Premises     each word's form and field are checked against its label's
                 distance (the control as a byte count, word 1 in
                 instructions, word 2 in bytes); the handler is still in place.
  BYTES needs word 1 in the sled at its byte reading and word 2 on its label;
  INSTRUCTIONS needs the reverse.  The two words differ, so they cannot both
  land on a label.

ARM B  Does a backward DJNZ x,##label land correctly in cog and in hub?
  The compiler emits AUGS + DJNZ with an 18-bit count (-303), the same words
  in cog and hub.  The cog case added as a positive offset lands in hub at
  PC + $3FED1; a hub sled there reports the address.  The cog's LUT is filled
  with CALL #\lutsled so a landing in LUT reports too.
    Controls     a forward ## DJNZ and a near 9-bit DJNZ, in cog and in hub,
                 each must land (loop counts exact).
    Readings     LABEL (two passes of the loop, x = 0, and none of the three
                 ADDs just before the label ran), or the hub sled at the
                 predicted address, or another reported address.
    Premises     the cog and hub words both hold the 18-bit instruction
                 count; the handler is still in place.

ARM C  Does a pending SETQ survive an instruction cancelled by a false
  condition, or by SKIP?  Four registers are filled with a sentinel and a
  plain RDLONG follows.  4 changed = SURVIVES, 1 changed = CONSUMED.
    Controls     adjacent SETQ #3 / RDLONG reads 4; plain RDLONG reads 1.
    Premise      the cancelled MOV writes x; x is cleared first and must
                 still be 0, else that case is a RIG FAIL.

ARM D  The same for AUGS and AUGD.  y = $0246_8BFF augmented, $1FF not.
    Controls     no cancelled instruction gives the augmented value; no
                 AUGS / AUGD gives $1FF.
    Premise      the cancelled MOV's x, and the LUT long the cancelled WRLUT
                 writes, are cleared first and must still be 0.

ARM E  Do CALLA/RETA, CALLB/RETB and CALLD/JMP PA suspend a skip pattern?
  SKIP #%101 before the call: bit 0 cancels an ADD to a marker, bit 1 is the
  call.  The subroutine adds 16 and 32, the code after the call adds 1, 2,
  4, 8.  The marker must still be 0 (the pattern was in force at the call),
  else RIG FAIL.  After the last ADD, GETBRK D WC gives the CALL depth since
  SKIP in D[31:28] (P2 Documentation, GETBRK); 0 means skipping has resumed.
    sub 48, main 15, depth > 0   SUSPENDED, the return did not resume the
                                 pattern (depth printed)
  A control with a non-zero depth is RIG FAIL.  Depth %1111 (the preset: the
  GETBRK did not run) is NO READING, and so is a non-zero depth beside a
  48,14 or 32,15 sum, which is not a consistent state.
    sub 48, main 14   SUSPENDED and resumed after the return
    sub 32, main 15   NOT SUSPENDED: the subroutine consumed the pattern
    sub 48, main 15   PATTERN ENDED at the call
    Controls     CALL/RET reads 48, 14 (the P2 Documentation's rule for
                 CALL); the same instructions inline, with no call, read
                 32, 15.

ARM F  Does ALTD / ALTS / ALTR apply past an instruction SKIP cancels?
  The instruction between the ALT and its target is ADD mark,#1, executed in
  one control and skipped in the case under test.
    Controls     no instruction between: the ALT applies to the target; an
                 executed ADD between: the ADD takes the ALT (its own
                 signature: base[idx] + 1, mark = base+idx, or base[idx] = 1).
    Premise      in the skip case mark must be 0 and the ADD's signature
                 absent, else RIG FAIL.
    Readings     APPLIES (base+idx changed, or x reads base+idx) or NOT
                 (x changed, or x reads y).

ARM G  Does a _RET_ SETQ2 #$A5 at the end of a bytecode routine leave Q for
  the next routine?  The next routine's first instruction is MUXQ.
    Controls     adjacent SETQ / MUXQ reads $A5; a QDIV with no SETQ before
                 it leaves Q at 0.
    Premises     bytecode 0's and bytecode 1's routines each set a marker;
                 bytecode 0 clears the value read, and MUXQ of that 0 with
                 all ones gives exactly Q.
    Readings     $A5 LEFT, the table long XBYTE read, 0, or OTHER.

ARM H  Does TRGINT1 branch while STALLI is active?  The ISR counts.
    Controls     no trigger counts 0; TRGINT1 with ALLOWI counts 1.
    Premise      GETBRK D WCZ: D[1] is 0 in the ALLOWI control and 1 just
                 after STALLI and TRGINT1 (P2 Documentation, GETBRK).
    Readings     (before ALLOWI, after) = (0,1) HELD, (1,1) BRANCHED,
                 (0,0) LOST.

NOT MEASURED
  SKIPF, hub execution of arms C to H, other CALLD registers, other XBYTE
  modes, INT2 and INT3.  One part, N = 1.
}

CON ' ---- Rig Parameters ----
  _clkfreq        = 200_000_000
  DEBUG_COGS      = %0000_0001

  REC_N           = 32
  R_DONE          = 0                   ' the worker writes DONE_V here last
  R_MODE          = 1                   ' which step the worker runs
  R_P1            = 2                   ' a hub address the step needs
  R_V             = 3                   ' first result long
  DONE_V          = $0D0E_0D0E
  SENT            = $5E5E_5E5E          ' "not written"
  STEP_MS         = 50
  STACK_ROOM      = 8_192               ' room kept above the program for the Spin2 stack

  HANDLER         = $0_FDA0             ' hub address every sled long calls
  SLED_W          = $FDA0_FDA0          ' CALL #\$0FDA0, the same word at a 2-byte offset
  SLEDB_LO        = $3_F000             ' hub sled for the cog-case landing of arm B
  SLEDB_LONGS     = 5_120               ' $3F000..$43FFF

  MK_LAND_C       = 1                   ' landing markers
  MK_LAND_D       = 2
  MK_LAND_H       = 3
  MK_SLED         = 4
  MK_FELL         = 5
  MK_LUT          = 6
  MK_LABEL        = 7
  MK_CTL          = 8

  L_LABEL         = 1                   ' landing classes
  L_PRED          = 2
  L_ELSE          = 3
  L_NONE          = 4

  A_KIND          = R_V
  A_ADDR          = R_V + 1
  B_KIND          = R_V
  B_ADDR          = R_V + 1
  B_HY            = R_V + 2             ' hits, or y in the controls
  B_XF            = R_V + 3             ' x, or the forward miss count
  BR_NEAR         = R_V + 4             ' near-branch loop count
  BR_SLOP         = R_V + 5             ' ADDs executed just before cogtop

  AUGV            = ($12345 << 9) | $1FF
  F_LS            = $0F0                ' LUT slots for arm D (an immediate LUT address stops at 255)
  F_LS2           = $0F1

  M_C             = 0                   ' worker steps of the flow image
  M_D             = 1
  M_E0            = 2
  M_E1            = 3
  M_E2            = 4
  M_E3            = 5
  M_E4            = 6
  M_F             = 7
  M_G             = 8
  M_H             = 9

  E_SUSP          = 1                   ' arm E readings
  E_NOT           = 2
  E_ENDED         = 3
  E_OTHER         = 4
  E_HUNG          = 5
  E_NOPAT         = 6
  E_DEEP          = 7
  E_SUSPNR        = 8
  E_NOGB          = 9

  XV              = $777                ' arm F register values
  YV              = $999
  BV2             = $BA5E_0002

VAR ' ---- Rig State ----
  long  rec[REC_N]
  long  estk[16]                        ' hub stack for CALLA and CALLB
  long  eDep[5]                         ' arm E CALL depth after each form's return
  long  guardEnd

PUB main()
'' Run arms A to H and print every reading and verdict.
''

  p0(string("=== test-contract-gaps-p1-instruction-flow ==="))
  if @guardEnd + STACK_ROOM > HANDLER
    p1(string("RIG FAIL: the program reaches the sled handler address"), @guardEnd)
  else
    arm_a()
    arm_b()
    arm_c()
    arm_d()
    arm_e()
    arm_f()
    arm_g()
    arm_h()
  p0(string("=== END ==="))
  debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")
  repeat

PRI launch(pImg, mode, p1v) : ok | cog, t0
' Run one step in a fresh worker cog and wait for its DONE.
'
' @param pImg - hub address of the worker image
' @param mode - the step number
' @param p1v - a hub address the step needs
' @returns ok - TRUE when the worker wrote DONE in time

' Local Variables:
' @local cog - the worker cog
' @local t0 - CT at the launch

  longfill(@rec, SENT, REC_N)
  rec[R_DONE] := 0
  rec[R_MODE] := mode
  rec[R_P1] := p1v
  cog := coginit(COGEXEC_NEW, pImg, @rec)
  if cog < 0
    p0(string("RIG FAIL: no free cog for a step"))
    return FALSE
  t0 := getct()
  repeat until rec[R_DONE] == DONE_V
    if getct() - t0 > clkfreq / 1000 * STEP_MS
      cogstop(cog)
      p1(string("STEP HUNG: no DONE within the step limit, mode"), mode)
      return FALSE
  cogstop(cog)
  ok := TRUE

PRI landing(ok, kind, retAddr, mkLabel, pred) : cls
' Classify where a branch landed.
'
' @param ok - the step finished
' @param kind - the marker the step wrote
' @param retAddr - return address a sled pushed (landing + 4 in hub)
' @param mkLabel - the marker of the label under test
' @param pred - the address the other reading predicts
' @returns cls - L_LABEL, L_PRED, L_ELSE or L_NONE

  cls := L_NONE
  if not ok
    return
  if kind == mkLabel
    cls := L_LABEL
  elseif kind == MK_SLED
    cls := (retAddr - 4 == pred) ? L_PRED : L_ELSE
  elseif kind == MK_LUT
    cls := L_ELSE

' ---------------------------------------------------------------- arm A

PRI arm_a() | ok0, ok1, ok2, k0, k1, k2, r1, r2, w0, w1, w2, f1, f2, eb, ei, s1, s2
' Far CALLD PA in hub: the compiler's word and a hand-encoded byte-offset word.
'

  long[HANDLER] := long[@a_handler]
  w0 := long[@a_e0]
  w1 := long[@a_e1]
  w2 := long[@a_hand]
  f1 := (w1 & $F_FFFF) signx 19
  f2 := (w2 & $F_FFFF) signx 19
  eb := @a_e1 + 4 + f1                  ' word 1 read as bytes
  ei := @a_hand + 4 + f2 * 4            ' word 2 read as instructions
  ok0 := launch(@a_entry, 0, @a_e0)
  k0 := rec[A_KIND]
  ok1 := launch(@a_entry, 1, @a_e1)
  k1 := rec[A_KIND]
  r1 := rec[A_ADDR]
  ok2 := launch(@a_entry, 2, @a_hand)
  k2 := rec[A_KIND]
  r2 := rec[A_ADDR]
  s1 := landing(ok1, k1, r1, MK_LAND_D, eb)
  s2 := landing(ok2, k2, r2, MK_LAND_H, ei)
  p3(string("A words: far CALL control, compiler CALLD, hand-encoded CALLD"), w0, w1, w2)
  p2(string("A fields: compiler, hand"), f1, f2)
  p2(string("A labels: compiler target, hand target"), @a_land_d, @a_land_h)
  p2(string("A predicted landings: word 1 as bytes, word 2 as instructions"), eb, ei)
  p2(string("A control far CALL: finished, marker"), ok0, k0)
  p4(string("A word 1: finished, marker, sled return, class"), ok1, k1, r1, s1)
  p4(string("A word 2: finished, marker, sled return, class"), ok2, k2, r2, s2)
  if not ok0
    pv(string("A"), string("NO READING, the far CALL control step hung"))
  elseif (w0 >> 20) <> $FDB or ((w0 & $F_FFFF) signx 19) <> @a_land_c - (@a_e0 + 4)
    pv(string("A"), string("RIG FAIL, the control is not a 20-bit relative CALL holding its label's byte distance"))
  elseif long[HANDLER] <> long[@a_handler]
    pv(string("A"), string("RIG FAIL, the sled handler was overwritten during the run"))
  elseif k0 <> MK_LAND_C
    pv(string("A"), string("RIG FAIL, the far CALL control did not land on its label"))
  elseif (w1 >> 20) <> $FE1 or f1 * 4 <> @a_land_d - (@a_e1 + 4)
    pv(string("A"), string("RIG FAIL, word 1 is not a 20-bit CALLD PA holding the label's distance in instructions"))
  elseif (w2 >> 20) <> $FE1 or f2 <> @a_land_h - (@a_hand + 4)
    pv(string("A"), string("RIG FAIL, word 2 is not a 20-bit CALLD PA holding the label's distance in bytes"))
  elseif s1 == L_PRED and s2 == L_LABEL
    pv(string("A"), string("BYTES, the CALLD field is a byte offset in hub: the compiler's word lands 1006 bytes back, not on its label"))
  elseif s1 == L_LABEL and s2 == L_PRED
    pv(string("A"), string("INSTRUCTIONS, the CALLD field counts instructions in hub: the compiler's word lands on its label"))
  else
    pv(string("A"), string("NO READING, the two words did not land as one reading predicts; see the raw lines"))

' ---------------------------------------------------------------- arm B

PRI arm_b() | okc, okh, ok1, ok3, cy, cf, cn, hy, hf, hn, k1, r1, h1, x1, sl1, k3, r3, h3, x3, f1, fh, pc1, ec, s1, s3, ctl
' Backward DJNZ with a ## target in cog and in hub, with its controls.
'

  longfill(SLEDB_LO, SLED_W, SLEDB_LONGS)
  long[HANDLER] := long[@b_handler]
  f1 := ((long[@b_bk] & $7F_FFFF) << 9) | (long[@b_bk + 4] & $1FF)
  fh := ((long[@b_hbk] & $7F_FFFF) << 9) | (long[@b_hbk + 4] & $1FF)
  pc1 := (@b_bk + 8 - @b_entry) >> 2
  ec := (pc1 + f1) & $F_FFFF            ' the cog case with the field added as-is

  okc := launch(@b_entry, 0, 0)
  cy := rec[B_HY]
  cf := rec[B_XF]
  cn := rec[BR_NEAR]
  okh := launch(@b_entry, 2, @b_hctl)
  hy := rec[B_HY]
  hf := rec[B_XF]
  hn := rec[BR_NEAR]
  ok1 := launch(@b_entry, 1, 0)
  k1 := rec[B_KIND]
  r1 := rec[B_ADDR]
  h1 := rec[B_HY]
  x1 := rec[B_XF]
  sl1 := rec[BR_SLOP]
  ok3 := launch(@b_entry, 3, @b_hback)
  k3 := rec[B_KIND]
  r3 := rec[B_ADDR]
  h3 := rec[B_HY]
  x3 := rec[B_XF]
  if k1 == MK_LABEL and (h1 <> 2 or x1 <> 0)
    k1 := MK_FELL                       ' reached the end, but not by two passes
  if k3 == MK_LABEL and (h3 <> 2 or x3 <> 0)
    k3 := MK_FELL
  s1 := landing(ok1, k1, r1, MK_LABEL, ec)
  s3 := landing(ok3, k3, r3, MK_LABEL, -1)

  p4(string("B cog words AUGS, DJNZ; hub words AUGS, DJNZ"), long[@b_bk], long[@b_bk + 4], long[@b_hbk], long[@b_hbk + 4])
  p3(string("B cog field, hub field, predicted cog landing as-is"), f1, fh, ec)
  p4(string("B cog controls: finished, y, forward misses, near count"), okc, cy, cf, cn)
  p4(string("B hub controls: finished, y, forward misses, near count"), okh, hy, hf, hn)
  p4(string("B cog backward: finished, marker, sled return, class"), ok1, k1, r1, s1)
  p3(string("B cog backward: passes, x, slop (ADDs just before the label, must be 0)"), h1, x1, sl1)
  p4(string("B hub backward: finished, marker, sled return, class"), ok3, k3, r3, s3)
  p2(string("B hub backward: passes, x"), h3, x3)
  ctl := cy == 1 and cf == 0 and cn == 2 and hy == 1 and hf == 0 and hn == 2
  if not okc or not okh
    pv(string("B"), string("NO READING, a control step hung"))
  elseif not ctl
    pv(string("B"), string("RIG FAIL, a forward ## or near DJNZ control did not land"))
  elseif f1 <> ((cogtop_addr() - pc1) & $3_FFFF)
    pv(string("B"), string("RIG FAIL, the cog word does not hold the 18-bit count this arm measures"))
  elseif fh <> (((@hubtop - (@b_hbk + 8)) / 4) & $3_FFFF)
    pv(string("B"), string("RIG FAIL, the hub word does not hold the 18-bit instruction count this arm measures"))
  elseif long[HANDLER] <> long[@b_handler]
    pv(string("B"), string("RIG FAIL, the sled handler was overwritten during the run"))
  else
    if s1 == L_LABEL and sl1 <> 0
      pv(string("B cog"), string("MISSES, lands 1 to 3 longs before its label (slop count above)"))
    elseif s1 == L_LABEL
      pv(string("B cog"), string("LANDS ON ITS LABEL"))
    elseif s1 == L_PRED
      pv(string("B cog"), string("MISSES, lands in hub at PC plus the field taken as a positive offset (address above)"))
    elseif s1 == L_ELSE and k1 == MK_LUT
      pv(string("B cog"), string("MISSES, lands in LUT; the address is the sled return minus 1"))
    elseif s1 == L_ELSE
      pv(string("B cog"), string("MISSES, lands in the hub sled at another address; the address is the sled return minus 4"))
    else
      pv(string("B cog"), string("NO READING, no landing marker; see the raw lines"))
    if s3 == L_LABEL
      pv(string("B hub"), string("LANDS ON ITS LABEL"))
    elseif s3 == L_ELSE
      pv(string("B hub"), string("MISSES, lands in a sled; see the sled return above"))
    else
      pv(string("B hub"), string("NO READING, no landing marker; see the raw lines"))

PRI cogtop_addr() : a
' The cog address of the cog-case loop top.
'
' @returns a - cog address of cogtop

  a := (@cogtop - @b_entry) >> 2

' ---------------------------------------------------------------- arm C

PRI c_count(i0) : n | i, v
' How many of four registers a RDLONG changed: 4, 1, or -1 for any other shape.
'
' @param i0 - index of the first of the four record longs
' @returns n - 4, 1 or -1

' Local Variables:
' @local i - register index
' @local v - the value read back

  n := 0
  repeat i from 0 to 3
    v := rec[i0 + i]
    if v == long[@c_data][i]
      n++
    elseif v <> SENT
      return -1
  if n == 1 and rec[i0] <> long[@c_data][0]
    n := -1
  elseif n <> 1 and n <> 4
    n := -1

PRI arm_c() | ok, n0, n1, n2, n3, x2, x3, i
' SETQ across a cancelled instruction.  Each cancelled MOV writes x if it
' runs; x is cleared first and must still be 0.
'

  ok := launch(@f_entry, M_C, @c_data)
  repeat i from 0 to 3
    p4(string("C step registers r0..r3"), rec[R_V + i * 4], rec[R_V + i * 4 + 1], rec[R_V + i * 4 + 2], rec[R_V + i * 4 + 3])
  n0 := c_count(R_V)
  n1 := c_count(R_V + 4)
  n2 := c_count(R_V + 8)
  n3 := c_count(R_V + 12)
  x2 := rec[R_V + 16]
  x3 := rec[R_V + 17]
  p4(string("C changed: adjacent, plain, false condition, SKIP"), n0, n1, n2, n3)
  p2(string("C cancelled MOV's x, must be 0: false condition, SKIP"), x2, x3)
  if not ok
    pv(string("C"), string("NO READING, step hung"))
  elseif n0 <> 4 or n1 <> 1
    pv(string("C"), string("RIG FAIL, the adjacent SETQ did not read 4 or the plain RDLONG did not read 1"))
  else
    say_case(string("C false condition"), x2, n2 == 4, n2 == 1)
    say_case(string("C SKIP"), x3, n3 == 4, n3 == 1)

PRI say_case(pArm, foot, bSurv, bCons)
' Print a SURVIVES / CONSUMED / OTHER verdict, or RIG FAIL when the
' instruction meant to be cancelled left its footprint.
'
' @param pArm - the arm and step name
' @param foot - what the cancelled instruction writes if it runs; 0 when cancelled
' @param bSurv - the survived reading was seen
' @param bCons - the consumed reading was seen

  if foot <> 0
    pv(pArm, string("RIG FAIL, the instruction meant to be cancelled executed (footprint above)"))
  elseif bSurv
    pv(pArm, string("SURVIVES, the pending prefix reached the next instruction"))
  elseif bCons
    pv(pArm, string("CONSUMED, the cancelled instruction took the pending prefix"))
  else
    pv(pArm, string("OTHER, see the raw lines"))

' ---------------------------------------------------------------- arm D

PRI arm_d() | ok
' AUGS and AUGD across a cancelled instruction.
'

  ok := launch(@f_entry, M_D, 0)
  p4(string("D AUGS y: control aug, control none, false condition, SKIP"), rec[R_V], rec[R_V + 1], rec[R_V + 2], rec[R_V + 3])
  p4(string("D AUGD y: control aug, control none, false condition, SKIP"), rec[R_V + 4], rec[R_V + 5], rec[R_V + 6], rec[R_V + 7])
  p4(string("D cancelled footprints, must be 0: AUGS x false, x SKIP; AUGD LUT false, LUT SKIP"), rec[R_V + 8], rec[R_V + 9], rec[R_V + 10], rec[R_V + 11])
  if not ok
    pv(string("D"), string("NO READING, step hung"))
  elseif rec[R_V] <> AUGV or rec[R_V + 1] <> $1FF or rec[R_V + 4] <> AUGV or rec[R_V + 5] <> $1FF
    pv(string("D"), string("RIG FAIL, a control did not read the augmented value and $1FF"))
  else
    say_case(string("D AUGS false condition"), rec[R_V + 8], rec[R_V + 2] == AUGV, rec[R_V + 2] == $1FF)
    say_case(string("D AUGS SKIP"), rec[R_V + 9], rec[R_V + 3] == AUGV, rec[R_V + 3] == $1FF)
    say_case(string("D AUGD false condition"), rec[R_V + 10], rec[R_V + 6] == AUGV, rec[R_V + 6] == $1FF)
    say_case(string("D AUGD SKIP"), rec[R_V + 11], rec[R_V + 7] == AUGV, rec[R_V + 7] == $1FF)

' ---------------------------------------------------------------- arm E

PRI e_step(mode, pName) : cls | ok, sb, mn, fl, pr, dp
' Run one call form under SKIP and classify it.
'
' @param mode - the worker step
' @param pName - the form's name
' @returns cls - E_SUSP, E_NOT, E_ENDED or E_OTHER

' Local Variables:
' @local ok - the step finished
' @local sb - subroutine marker sum
' @local mn - main marker sum
' @local fl - 1 when the return fell through
' @local pr - the bit-0 marker, 0 when the pattern was in force
' @local dp - CALL depth since SKIP after the return, from GETBRK WC D[31:28]

  ok := launch(@f_entry, mode, @estk)
  sb := rec[R_V]
  mn := rec[R_V + 1]
  fl := rec[R_V + 2]
  pr := rec[R_V + 3]
  dp := (rec[R_V + 4] >> 28) & $F
  eDep[mode - M_E0] := dp
  p4(pName, ok, sb, mn, fl)
  p1(string("  marker on pattern bit 0 (0 = the pattern was in force at the call)"), pr)
  p3(string("  GETBRK WC after the return: D, CALL depth D[31:28] (0 = skipping resumed), C"), rec[R_V + 4], dp, rec[R_V + 5])
  cls := E_OTHER
  if not ok
    cls := E_HUNG
  elseif pr <> 0
    cls := E_NOPAT
  elseif fl == 0
    if sb == 48 and mn == 14
      cls := E_SUSP
    elseif sb == 32 and mn == 15
      cls := E_NOT
    elseif sb == 48 and mn == 15
      cls := E_ENDED
    if cls <> E_OTHER and dp == $F
      cls := E_NOGB                     ' GETBRK never ran: the preset depth is still there
    elseif cls == E_ENDED and dp <> 0
      cls := E_SUSPNR                   ' full sub sum and a raised depth: suspended, not resumed
    elseif cls <> E_OTHER and dp <> 0
      cls := E_DEEP                     ' a raised depth beside 48,14 or 32,15 is not a consistent state

PRI arm_e() | c0, c1, ca, cb, cd
' Call forms under a skip pattern.
'

  c0 := e_step(M_E0, string("E CALL/RET control: finished, sub sum, main sum, fell through"))
  c1 := e_step(M_E1, string("E inline control: finished, sub sum, main sum, fell through"))
  ca := e_step(M_E2, string("E CALLA/RETA: finished, sub sum, main sum, fell through"))
  cb := e_step(M_E3, string("E CALLB/RETB: finished, sub sum, main sum, fell through"))
  cd := e_step(M_E4, string("E CALLD/JMP PA: finished, sub sum, main sum, fell through"))
  if c0 == E_HUNG or c1 == E_HUNG
    pv(string("E"), string("NO READING, a control step hung"))
  elseif c0 == E_NOGB or c1 == E_NOGB
    pv(string("E"), string("NO READING, a control's GETBRK did not run"))
  elseif c0 == E_DEEP or c1 == E_DEEP or c0 == E_SUSPNR or c1 == E_SUSPNR
    pv(string("E"), string("RIG FAIL, a control's CALL depth was not 0 after its return"))
  elseif c0 <> E_SUSP or c1 <> E_NOT
    pv(string("E"), string("RIG FAIL, CALL did not read 48,14 or the inline control did not read 32,15"))
  else
    say_e(string("E CALLA/RETA"), ca, eDep[M_E2 - M_E0])
    say_e(string("E CALLB/RETB"), cb, eDep[M_E3 - M_E0])
    say_e(string("E CALLD/JMP PA"), cd, eDep[M_E4 - M_E0])

PRI say_e(pArm, cls, dp)
' Print an arm E verdict.
'
' @param pArm - the call form
' @param cls - its class
' @param dp - its CALL depth after the return

  case cls
    E_SUSPNR: pvv(pArm, string("SUSPENDED, the return did not resume the pattern (depth)"), dp)
    E_DEEP:  pvv(pArm, string("NO READING, a raised CALL depth beside a 48,14 or 32,15 sum is not a consistent state (depth)"), dp)
    E_NOGB:  pv(pArm, string("NO READING, the GETBRK after the return did not run"))
    E_SUSP:  pv(pArm, string("SUSPENDED, the subroutine ran whole and the pattern resumed after the return"))
    E_NOT:   pv(pArm, string("NOT SUSPENDED, the subroutine's instructions consumed the pattern"))
    E_ENDED: pv(pArm, string("PATTERN ENDED, the subroutine ran whole and nothing after the return was skipped"))
    E_HUNG:  pv(pArm, string("NO READING, step hung"))
    E_NOPAT: pv(pArm, string("RIG FAIL, the skip pattern was not in force at the call"))
    other:   pv(pArm, string("OTHER, see the raw lines"))

' ---------------------------------------------------------------- arm F

PRI f_cls(kind, b2, x, mark) : cls | a2
' Classify one ALT step: 1 applies to the final instruction, 2 does not,
' 3 the in-between ADD f_mark,#1 ran and took the ALT, 0 other.
'
' @param kind - 0 ALTD, 1 ALTS, 2 ALTR
' @param b2 - base[idx] after the step
' @param x - x after the step
' @param mark - f_mark after the step (cleared to 0 first)
' @returns cls - 0..3

' Local Variables:
' @local a2 - cog address of base[idx], what ALTS puts in the ADD's S field

  a2 := (@f_b2 - @f_entry) >> 2
  cls := 0
  case kind
    0:
      if b2 == 7 and x == XV and mark == 0
        cls := 1
      elseif b2 == BV2 and x == 7 and mark == 0
        cls := 2
      elseif b2 == BV2 + 1 and x == 7 and mark == 0
        cls := 3
    1:
      if b2 == BV2 and x == BV2 and mark == 0
        cls := 1
      elseif b2 == BV2 and x == YV and mark == 0
        cls := 2
      elseif b2 == BV2 and x == YV and mark == a2
        cls := 3
    2:
      if b2 == XV + 7 and x == XV and mark == 0
        cls := 1
      elseif b2 == BV2 and x == XV + 7 and mark == 0
        cls := 2
      elseif b2 == 1 and x == XV + 7 and mark == 0
        cls := 3

PRI arm_f() | ok, k, i, c0, c1, c2, pName
' ALTD, ALTS and ALTR past a skipped instruction.  The instruction between
' the ALT and its target is ADD f_mark,#1 in the control and in the skip
' case, so whether it ran shows.
'

  ok := launch(@f_entry, M_F, 0)
  repeat k from 0 to 2
    i := R_V + k * 9
    pName := lookupz(k: string("F ALTD"), string("F ALTS"), string("F ALTR"))
    p0(pName)
    p3(string("  base[idx], x, mark: nothing between"), rec[i], rec[i + 1], rec[i + 2])
    p3(string("  base[idx], x, mark: ADD between, executed"), rec[i + 3], rec[i + 4], rec[i + 5])
    p3(string("  base[idx], x, mark: ADD between, skipped"), rec[i + 6], rec[i + 7], rec[i + 8])
    c0 := f_cls(k, rec[i], rec[i + 1], rec[i + 2])
    c1 := f_cls(k, rec[i + 3], rec[i + 4], rec[i + 5])
    c2 := f_cls(k, rec[i + 6], rec[i + 7], rec[i + 8])
    p3(string("  classes (1 applies, 2 not, 3 the ADD took it, 0 other)"), c0, c1, c2)
    if not ok
      pv(pName, string("NO READING, step hung"))
    elseif c0 <> 1 or c1 <> 3
      pv(pName, string("RIG FAIL, the no-skip control did not apply or the executed ADD did not take the ALT"))
    elseif c2 == 3 or rec[i + 8] <> 0
      pv(pName, string("RIG FAIL, the instruction meant to be skipped executed"))
    elseif c2 == 1
      pv(pName, string("APPLIES past the skipped instruction"))
    elseif c2 == 2
      pv(pName, string("DOES NOT APPLY past the skipped instruction"))
    else
      pv(pName, string("OTHER, see the raw lines"))

' ---------------------------------------------------------------- arm G

PRI arm_g() | ok, q1, q2, lt, qx, seen, gran
' Q across an XBYTE bytecode boundary after _RET_ SETQ2.
'

  ok := launch(@f_entry, M_G, @g_code)
  q1 := rec[R_V]
  q2 := rec[R_V + 1]
  lt := rec[R_V + 2]
  qx := rec[R_V + 3]
  seen := rec[R_V + 4]
  gran := rec[R_V + 5]
  p4(string("G controls: adjacent MUXQ, after QDIV; table long; next routine MUXQ"), q1, q2, lt, qx)
  p2(string("G routines ran: bytecode 0 (the _RET_ SETQ2), bytecode 1"), gran, seen)
  if not ok
    pv(string("G"), string("NO READING, step hung"))
  elseif gran <> 1 or seen <> 1
    pv(string("G"), string("RIG FAIL, bytecode 0's or bytecode 1's routine did not run"))
  elseif q1 <> $A5 or q2 <> 0 or lt == $A5 or lt == 0 or lt == SENT
    pv(string("G"), string("RIG FAIL, a Q control missed or the table long is not distinct"))
  elseif qx == $A5
    pv(string("G"), string("LEFT, the next bytecode's routine reads Q = $A5"))
  elseif qx == lt
    pv(string("G"), string("REPLACED, Q holds the table long XBYTE read for the next bytecode"))
  elseif qx == 0
    pv(string("G"), string("ZEROED, the next routine reads Q = 0"))
  else
    pv(string("G"), string("OTHER, see the raw line"))

' ---------------------------------------------------------------- arm H

PRI arm_h() | ok, n0, c0, cb, ca
' TRGINT1 while STALLI is active.
'

  ok := launch(@f_entry, M_H, 0)
  n0 := rec[R_V]
  c0 := rec[R_V + 1]
  cb := rec[R_V + 2]
  ca := rec[R_V + 3]
  p4(string("H ISR counts: no trigger, ALLOWI trigger, STALLI before ALLOWI, after"), n0, c0, cb, ca)
  p2(string("H GETBRK status (bit 1 = STALLI mode): in the ALLOWI control, after STALLI and TRGINT1"), rec[R_V + 4], rec[R_V + 5])
  if not ok
    pv(string("H"), string("NO READING, step hung"))
  elseif (rec[R_V + 4] & %10) <> 0 or (rec[R_V + 5] & %10) == 0
    pv(string("H"), string("RIG FAIL, GETBRK did not show ALLOWI in the control and STALLI at the trigger"))
  elseif n0 <> 0 or c0 <> 1
    pv(string("H"), string("RIG FAIL, the ISR ran with no trigger or did not run on TRGINT1 with ALLOWI"))
  elseif cb == 0 and ca == 1
    pv(string("H"), string("HELD, TRGINT1 under STALLI branches only after ALLOWI"))
  elseif cb == 1 and ca == 1
    pv(string("H"), string("BRANCHED, TRGINT1 branches while STALLI is active"))
  elseif cb == 0 and ca == 0
    pv(string("H"), string("LOST, a TRGINT1 under STALLI never branches"))
  else
    pv(string("H"), string("OTHER, see the raw line"))

' ---------------------------------------------------------------- printing

PRI p0(pS)
' Print a hub string.
'
' @param pS - the string

  debug(zstr_(pS))

PRI p1(pS, a)
' Print a hub string and one value.
'
' @param pS - the string
' @param a - the value

  debug(zstr_(pS), " ", uhex_long_(a))

PRI p2(pS, a, b)
' Print a hub string and two values.
'
' @param pS - the string
' @param a - first value
' @param b - second value

  debug(zstr_(pS), " ", uhex_long_(a), " ", uhex_long_(b))

PRI p3(pS, a, b, c)
' Print a hub string and three values.
'
' @param pS - the string
' @param a - first value
' @param b - second value
' @param c - third value

  debug(zstr_(pS), " ", uhex_long_(a), " ", uhex_long_(b), " ", uhex_long_(c))

PRI p4(pS, a, b, c, d)
' Print a hub string and four values.
'
' @param pS - the string
' @param a - first value
' @param b - second value
' @param c - third value
' @param d - fourth value

  debug(zstr_(pS), " ", uhex_long_(a), " ", uhex_long_(b), " ", uhex_long_(c), " ", uhex_long_(d))

PRI pv(pArm, pText)
' Print one verdict line.
'
' @param pArm - the arm
' @param pText - the verdict

  debug("VERDICT ", zstr_(pArm), ": ", zstr_(pText))

PRI pvv(pArm, pText, v)
' Print one verdict line with its raw value.
'
' @param pArm - the arm
' @param pText - the verdict
' @param v - the raw value

  debug("VERDICT ", zstr_(pArm), ": ", zstr_(pText), " ", uhex_long_(v))

DAT ' ---- arm A worker: the cog side ----
                alignl
                org     0
a_entry         rdlong  a_t, ptra[R_P1]
                jmp     a_t                     ' into hub at the step's entry
a_finish        wrlong  a_donev, ptra
                jmp     #$
a_sledhit       pop     a_t                     ' the sled's return address
                and     a_t, a_m20
                wrlong  a_t, ptra[A_ADDR]
                wrlong  #MK_SLED, ptra[A_KIND]
                jmp     #a_finish
a_fell          wrlong  #MK_FELL, ptra[A_KIND]
                jmp     #a_finish
a_t             long    0
a_donev         long    DONE_V
a_m20           long    $F_FFFF

' ---- arm A: the hub side ----
                orgh
                alignl
a_sledh         long    SLED_W[64]              ' catches word 2 read as instructions
a_land_h        wrlong  #MK_LAND_H, ptra[A_KIND]
                jmp     #\a_finish
                long    SLED_W[13]
a_hand          long    $FE10_0000 | ((a_land_h - ($ + 4)) & $F_FFFF)  ' CALLD PA,#rel, field in bytes
                jmp     #\a_fell
a_land_c        wrlong  #MK_LAND_C, ptra[A_KIND]
                ret
a_land_d        wrlong  #MK_LAND_D, ptra[A_KIND]
                jmp     #\a_finish
a_gap           long    SLED_W[1001]            ' catches word 1 read as bytes
a_e0            call    #a_land_c               ' control: far CALL
                jmp     #\a_finish
a_e1            calld   pa, #a_land_d           ' the compiler's far CALLD
                jmp     #\a_fell
a_handler       jmp     #\a_sledhit             ' copied to HANDLER at run time

DAT ' ---- arm B worker: the cog side ----
                alignl
                org     0
b_entry         jmp     #\b_setup               ' $000
                add     b_slop, #1              ' a landing 1 to 3 longs early counts here
                add     b_slop, #1
                add     b_slop, #1
cogtop          add     b_hits, #1              ' $004
                long    0[300]
b_bk            djnz    b_x, ##cogtop           ' backward, augmented, in cog
                jmp     #\b_report
b_hits          long    0
b_y             long    0
b_x             long    0                       ' $136
b_setup         rdlong  b_mode, ptra[R_MODE]
                rdlong  b_p1, ptra[R_P1]
                mov     b_i, #0
                rep     @.lf, ##512             ' a LUT landing calls b_lutsled
                wrlut   b_lutw, b_i
                add     b_i, #1
.lf             cmp     b_mode, #0      wz
        if_z    jmp     #b_m0
                cmp     b_mode, #1      wz
        if_z    jmp     #b_m1
                jmp     b_p1                    ' modes 2 and 3 run in hub
b_m0            mov     b_y, #2
                mov     b_fm, #0
                djnz    b_y, ##b_fwd            ' forward, augmented
                add     b_fm, #1
b_fwd           mov     b_z, #2
                mov     b_nh, #0
b_ntop          add     b_nh, #1
                djnz    b_z, #b_ntop            ' near, 9-bit
b_ctlout        wrlong  b_y, ptra[B_HY]
                wrlong  b_fm, ptra[B_XF]
                wrlong  b_nh, ptra[BR_NEAR]
                wrlong  #MK_CTL, ptra[B_KIND]
                jmp     #b_finish
b_m1            mov     b_x, #2
                mov     b_hits, #0
                mov     b_slop, #0
                jmp     #cogtop
b_report        wrlong  b_hits, ptra[B_HY]
                wrlong  b_x, ptra[B_XF]
                wrlong  b_slop, ptra[BR_SLOP]
                wrlong  #MK_LABEL, ptra[B_KIND]
                jmp     #b_finish
b_sledhit       pop     b_t
                and     b_t, b_m20
                wrlong  b_t, ptra[B_ADDR]
                wrlong  b_hits, ptra[B_HY]
                wrlong  b_x, ptra[B_XF]
                wrlong  #MK_SLED, ptra[B_KIND]
                jmp     #b_finish
b_lutsled       pop     b_t
                and     b_t, b_m20
                wrlong  b_t, ptra[B_ADDR]
                wrlong  b_hits, ptra[B_HY]
                wrlong  b_x, ptra[B_XF]
                wrlong  #MK_LUT, ptra[B_KIND]
b_finish        wrlong  b_donev, ptra
                jmp     #$
b_lutw          call    #\b_lutsled             ' the LUT sled word
b_mode          long    0
b_slop          long    0
b_p1            long    0
b_i             long    0
b_t             long    0
b_fm            long    0
b_z             long    0
b_nh            long    0
b_donev         long    DONE_V
b_m20           long    $F_FFFF

' ---- arm B: the hub side ----
                orgh
                alignl
b_hctl          mov     b_y, #2
                mov     b_fm, #0
                djnz    b_y, ##b_hfwd           ' forward, augmented, in hub
                add     b_fm, #1
b_hfwd          mov     b_z, #2
                mov     b_nh, #0
b_hntop         add     b_nh, #1
                djnz    b_z, #b_hntop           ' near, 9-bit, in hub
                jmp     #\b_ctlout
b_hback         mov     b_x, #2
                mov     b_hits, #0
hubtop          add     b_hits, #1
                long    0[300]
b_hbk           djnz    b_x, ##hubtop           ' backward, augmented, in hub
                jmp     #\b_report
b_handler       jmp     #\b_sledhit             ' copied to HANDLER at run time

DAT ' ---- arms C to H worker ----
                alignl
                org     0
f_entry         mov     f_rec, ptra
                mov     f_wp, ptra
                add     f_wp, #R_V * 4
                rdlong  f_mode, ptra[R_MODE]
                rdlong  f_p1, ptra[R_P1]
                cmp     f_mode, #M_C    wz
        if_z    jmp     #f_c
                cmp     f_mode, #M_D    wz
        if_z    jmp     #f_d
                cmp     f_mode, #M_E0   wz
        if_z    jmp     #f_e0
                cmp     f_mode, #M_E1   wz
        if_z    jmp     #f_e1
                cmp     f_mode, #M_E2   wz
        if_z    jmp     #f_e2
                cmp     f_mode, #M_E3   wz
        if_z    jmp     #f_e3
                cmp     f_mode, #M_E4   wz
        if_z    jmp     #f_e4
                cmp     f_mode, #M_F    wz
        if_z    jmp     #f_f
                cmp     f_mode, #M_G    wz
        if_z    jmp     #f_g
                cmp     f_mode, #M_H    wz
        if_z    jmp     #f_h
                jmp     #f_done

' arm C: four RDLONG shapes into f_r0..f_r3
f_c             call    #f_cfill
                setq    #3                      ' adjacent: reads 4
                rdlong  f_r0, f_p1
                call    #f_cput
                call    #f_cfill
                rdlong  f_r0, f_p1              ' plain: reads 1
                call    #f_cput
                call    #f_cfill
                mov     f_x, #0                 ' x stays 0 unless the cancelled MOV runs
                modc    _clr            wc
                setq    #3
        if_c    mov     f_x, #1                 ' cancelled by a false condition
                rdlong  f_r0, f_p1
                mov     f_fp0, f_x
                call    #f_cput
                call    #f_cfill
                mov     f_x, #0
                skip    #%10
                setq    #3
                mov     f_x, #2                 ' cancelled by SKIP
                rdlong  f_r0, f_p1
                mov     f_fp1, f_x
                call    #f_cput
                setq    #1                      ' the two footprints
                wrlong  f_fp0, f_wp
                jmp     #f_done

f_cfill         mov     f_r0, f_sent
                mov     f_r1, f_sent
                mov     f_r2, f_sent
        _ret_   mov     f_r3, f_sent

f_cput          setq    #3
                wrlong  f_r0, f_wp
        _ret_   add     f_wp, #16

' arm D: AUGS then AUGD
f_d             augs    #$12345                 ' control: augmented
                mov     f_y, #$1FF
                call    #f_put1
                mov     f_y, #$1FF              ' control: not augmented
                call    #f_put1
                mov     f_x, #0                 ' x stays 0 unless the cancelled MOV runs
                modc    _clr            wc
                augs    #$12345
        if_c    mov     f_x, #3                 ' cancelled by a false condition
                mov     f_y, #$1FF
                mov     f_fp0, f_x
                call    #f_put1
                mov     f_x, #0
                skip    #%10
                augs    #$12345
                mov     f_x, #3                 ' cancelled by SKIP
                mov     f_y, #$1FF
                mov     f_fp1, f_x
                call    #f_put1
                augd    #$12345                 ' control: augmented
                wrlut   #$1FF, #F_LS
                rdlut   f_y, #F_LS
                call    #f_put1
                wrlut   #$1FF, #F_LS            ' control: not augmented
                rdlut   f_y, #F_LS
                call    #f_put1
                wrlut   #0, #F_LS2              ' LUT[F_LS2] stays 0 unless the cancelled WRLUT runs
                modc    _clr            wc
                augd    #$12345
        if_c    wrlut   #3, #F_LS2              ' cancelled by a false condition
                wrlut   #$1FF, #F_LS
                rdlut   f_y, #F_LS
                rdlut   f_fp2, #F_LS2
                call    #f_put1
                wrlut   #0, #F_LS2
                skip    #%10
                augd    #$12345
                wrlut   #3, #F_LS2              ' cancelled by SKIP
                wrlut   #$1FF, #F_LS
                rdlut   f_y, #F_LS
                rdlut   f_fp3, #F_LS2
                call    #f_put1
                setq    #3                      ' the four footprints
                wrlong  f_fp0, f_wp
                jmp     #f_done

f_put1          wrlong  f_y, f_wp
        _ret_   add     f_wp, #4

' arm E: one call form per step.  Pattern %101: bit 0 cancels the ADD to
' f_pre (which shows the pattern is in force), bit 1 runs the call, bit 2 is
' the only other 1.  GETBRK WC after the last marker, where no model skips,
' records the CALL depth since SKIP: 0 when skipping has resumed.
f_e0            mov     f_sub, #0
                mov     f_main, #0
                mov     f_pre, #0
                neg     f_dep, #1               ' depth reads %1111 unless GETBRK runs
                skip    #%101
                add     f_pre, #1
                call    #\f_subc
                add     f_main, #1
                add     f_main, #2
                add     f_main, #4
                add     f_main, #8
                getbrk  f_dep           wc      ' D[31:28] = CALL depth since SKIP; C = next pattern bit
                wrc     f_depc
                jmp     #f_eout

f_e1            mov     f_sub, #0
                mov     f_main, #0
                mov     f_pre, #0
                neg     f_dep, #1               ' depth reads %1111 unless GETBRK runs
                skip    #%101
                add     f_pre, #1
                nop                             ' where the call would be
                add     f_sub, #16
                add     f_sub, #32
                nop                             ' where the return would be
                add     f_main, #1
                add     f_main, #2
                add     f_main, #4
                add     f_main, #8
                getbrk  f_dep           wc      ' D[31:28] = CALL depth since SKIP; C = next pattern bit
                wrc     f_depc
                jmp     #f_eout

f_e2            mov     f_sub, #0
                mov     f_main, #0
                mov     ptra, f_p1              ' hub stack
                mov     f_pre, #0
                neg     f_dep, #1               ' depth reads %1111 unless GETBRK runs
                skip    #%101
                add     f_pre, #1
                calla   #\f_suba
                add     f_main, #1
                add     f_main, #2
                add     f_main, #4
                add     f_main, #8
                getbrk  f_dep           wc      ' D[31:28] = CALL depth since SKIP; C = next pattern bit
                wrc     f_depc
                jmp     #f_eout

f_e3            mov     f_sub, #0
                mov     f_main, #0
                mov     ptrb, f_p1              ' hub stack
                mov     f_pre, #0
                neg     f_dep, #1               ' depth reads %1111 unless GETBRK runs
                skip    #%101
                add     f_pre, #1
                callb   #\f_subb
                add     f_main, #1
                add     f_main, #2
                add     f_main, #4
                add     f_main, #8
                getbrk  f_dep           wc      ' D[31:28] = CALL depth since SKIP; C = next pattern bit
                wrc     f_depc
                jmp     #f_eout

f_e4            mov     f_sub, #0
                mov     f_main, #0
                mov     f_pre, #0
                neg     f_dep, #1               ' depth reads %1111 unless GETBRK runs
                skip    #%101
                add     f_pre, #1
                calld   pa, #\f_subd
                add     f_main, #1
                add     f_main, #2
                add     f_main, #4
                add     f_main, #8
                getbrk  f_dep           wc      ' D[31:28] = CALL depth since SKIP; C = next pattern bit
                wrc     f_depc
                jmp     #f_eout

f_subc          add     f_sub, #16
                add     f_sub, #32
                ret
                jmp     #f_efell
f_suba          add     f_sub, #16
                add     f_sub, #32
                reta
                jmp     #f_efell
f_subb          add     f_sub, #16
                add     f_sub, #32
                retb
                jmp     #f_efell
f_subd          add     f_sub, #16
                add     f_sub, #32
                jmp     pa
                jmp     #f_efell

f_eout          mov     ptra, f_rec
                wrlong  f_sub, ptra[R_V]
                wrlong  f_main, ptra[R_V + 1]
                wrlong  #0, ptra[R_V + 2]
                wrlong  f_pre, ptra[R_V + 3]
                wrlong  f_dep, ptra[R_V + 4]
                wrlong  f_depc, ptra[R_V + 5]
                jmp     #f_done
f_efell         mov     ptra, f_rec
                wrlong  f_sub, ptra[R_V]
                wrlong  f_main, ptra[R_V + 1]
                wrlong  #1, ptra[R_V + 2]
                wrlong  f_pre, ptra[R_V + 3]
                wrlong  f_dep, ptra[R_V + 4]
                wrlong  f_depc, ptra[R_V + 5]
                jmp     #f_done

' arm F: base[idx] and x after each step
f_f             call    #f_finit
                altd    f_idx, #f_b0            ' ALTD, no skip
                mov     f_x, #7
                call    #f_fput
                call    #f_finit
                altd    f_idx, #f_b0            ' ALTD, an executed ADD between
                add     f_mark, #1
                mov     f_x, #7
                call    #f_fput
                call    #f_finit
                skip    #%10
                altd    f_idx, #f_b0            ' ALTD, a skipped ADD between
                add     f_mark, #1
                mov     f_x, #7
                call    #f_fput

                call    #f_finit
                alts    f_idx, #f_b0            ' ALTS, no skip
                mov     f_x, f_y
                call    #f_fput
                call    #f_finit
                alts    f_idx, #f_b0            ' ALTS, an executed ADD between
                add     f_mark, #1
                mov     f_x, f_y
                call    #f_fput
                call    #f_finit
                skip    #%10
                alts    f_idx, #f_b0            ' ALTS, a skipped ADD between
                add     f_mark, #1
                mov     f_x, f_y
                call    #f_fput

                call    #f_finit
                altr    f_idx, #f_b0            ' ALTR, no skip
                add     f_x, #7
                call    #f_fput
                call    #f_finit
                altr    f_idx, #f_b0            ' ALTR, an executed ADD between
                add     f_mark, #1
                add     f_x, #7
                call    #f_fput
                call    #f_finit
                skip    #%10
                altr    f_idx, #f_b0            ' ALTR, a skipped ADD between
                add     f_mark, #1
                add     f_x, #7
                call    #f_fput
                jmp     #f_done

f_finit         mov     f_b0, f_bv0
                mov     f_b1, f_bv1
                mov     f_b2, f_bv2
                mov     f_b3, f_bv3
                mov     f_x, f_xv
                mov     f_mark, #0
        _ret_   mov     f_y, f_yv

f_fput          wrlong  f_b2, f_wp
                add     f_wp, #4
                wrlong  f_x, f_wp
                add     f_wp, #4
                wrlong  f_mark, f_wp
        _ret_   add     f_wp, #4

' arm G: two Q controls, then three bytecodes under XBYTE
f_g             mov     f_q1, #0
                setq    #$A5
                muxq    f_q1, f_ones            ' control: adjacent, reads $A5
                wrlong  f_q1, f_wp
                add     f_wp, #4
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                qdiv    f_n, f_dv               ' no SETQ before it
                getqx   f_t
                getqy   f_t
                mov     f_q2, #0
                muxq    f_q2, f_ones            ' control: reads 0
                wrlong  f_q2, f_wp
                add     f_wp, #4
                wrlut   f_lset, #$080
                wrlut   f_lread, #$081
                wrlut   f_lhalt, #$082
                wrlong  f_lread, f_wp           ' the table long for bytecode 1
                add     f_wp, #4
                mov     f_gseen, #0
                rdfast  #0, f_p1
                push    #$1FF
        _ret_   setq    #$A4                    ' XBYTE: 7-bit index, table at LUT $080

f_gset          mov     f_gran, #1              ' bytecode 0: this routine ran
                mov     f_qx, #0
        _ret_   setq2   #$A5                    ' next bytecode only: same mode with F set
f_gread         muxq    f_qx, f_ones            ' bytecode 1: the routine's first instruction
        _ret_   mov     f_gseen, #1
f_ghalt         pop     f_t                     ' bytecode 2: leave XBYTE
                wrlong  f_qx, f_wp
                add     f_wp, #4
                wrlong  f_gseen, f_wp
                add     f_wp, #4
                wrlong  f_gran, f_wp
                jmp     #f_done

' arm H: interrupt counts
f_h             mov     ijmp1, #f_isr
                setint1 #0
                mov     f_ic, #0
                long    0[16]                   ' no trigger
                wrlong  f_ic, f_wp
                add     f_wp, #4
                mov     f_ic, #0
                trgint1                         ' control: ALLOWI is in force
                long    0[16]
                getbrk  f_br0           wcz     ' D[1] = 0 in ALLOWI mode
                wrlong  f_ic, f_wp
                add     f_wp, #4
                mov     f_ic, #0
                stalli
                trgint1
                getbrk  f_br1           wcz     ' D[1] = 1 in STALLI mode
                long    0[16]
                mov     f_cb, f_ic
                allowi
                long    0[16]
                mov     f_ca, f_ic
                wrlong  f_cb, f_wp
                add     f_wp, #4
                wrlong  f_ca, f_wp
                add     f_wp, #4
                wrlong  f_br0, f_wp
                add     f_wp, #4
                wrlong  f_br1, f_wp
                jmp     #f_done

f_isr           add     f_ic, #1
                reti1

f_done          mov     ptra, f_rec
                wrlong  f_donev, ptra
                jmp     #$

f_rec           long    0
f_wp            long    0
f_mode          long    0
f_p1            long    0
f_t             long    0
f_x             long    0
f_y             long    0
f_r0            long    0                       ' f_r0..f_r3 are one block
f_r1            long    0
f_r2            long    0
f_r3            long    0
f_sent          long    SENT
f_fp0           long    0                       ' f_fp0..f_fp3: footprints of cancelled instructions
f_fp1           long    0
f_fp2           long    0
f_fp3           long    0
f_mark          long    0
f_pre           long    0
f_dep           long    0
f_depc          long    0
f_gran          long    0
f_br0           long    0
f_br1           long    0
f_sub           long    0
f_main          long    0
f_b0            long    0                       ' f_b0..f_b3 are base[0..3]
f_b1            long    0
f_b2            long    0
f_b3            long    0
f_idx           long    2
f_bv0           long    $BA5E_0000
f_bv1           long    $BA5E_0001
f_bv2           long    BV2
f_bv3           long    $BA5E_0003
f_xv            long    XV
f_yv            long    YV
f_ones          long    $FFFF_FFFF
f_q1            long    0
f_q2            long    0
f_qx            long    SENT                    ' none of $A5, 0 or the table long
f_gseen         long    0
f_n             long    1000
f_dv            long    3
f_lset          long    f_gset
f_lread         long    f_gread
f_lhalt         long    f_ghalt
f_ic            long    0
f_cb            long    0
f_ca            long    0
f_donev         long    DONE_V

DAT ' ---- hub data ----
                orgh
                alignl
c_data          long    $C0DE_0001, $C0DE_0002, $C0DE_0003, $C0DE_0004, $C0DE_0005
g_code          byte    0, 1, 2, 2
